@startuml
title Configuration Anomaly Detection (CAD) - Architecture Overview

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

' External sources and users
rectangle "Alerting System\n(external)" as Alert
rectangle "SRE / Operations User" as SRE
rectangle "Deployment Engineer" as Deploy
rectangle "Developer / Contributor" as Dev

' CLI runtime container and library
node "CLI Runtime Container\nUBI minimal\ncontains /bin/cadctl" as Runtime {
  component "cadctl CLI" as CLI
  package "Integration Library" as IntLib {
    component "PagerDuty Integration" as PD
    component "AWS Integration" as AWS
    component "OCM Integration" as OCM
  }
}

' Tekton orchestration (default namespace)
node "Tekton (configuration-anomaly-detection namespace)" as Tekton {
  component "EventListener" as EL
  component "Trigger" as TR
  component "cad-checks-pipeline" as PIPE
  component "PipelineRun" as PR
}

' Direct execution helper (skip-webhook)
component "Skip-Webhook Direct Executor\n(create PipelineRun directly)" as DirectExec

' Template update utility and artifacts
component "Template Update Utility" as TmplUtil
folder "Deployment Template Artifacts\n(YAML manifests)" as Templates

' Data artifact
artifact "payload (JSON)\ncontains event.data.id" as Payload

' External operations systems
cloud "PagerDuty" as ExtPD
cloud "AWS" as ExtAWS
cloud "OCM" as ExtOCM

' Relationships: webhook-driven path
Alert --> EL : alert webhook
EL --> TR : event delivery
TR --> PR : create PipelineRun
PR --> PIPE : reference pipeline

' Execution of CAD checks using CLI inside pipeline tasks
PR ..> CLI : execute CAD checks\n(container steps)
CLI --> PD : communications/alerts
CLI --> AWS
CLI --> OCM

' Direct path (skip-webhook)
SRE --> DirectExec : invoke direct execution
DirectExec --> PR : create PipelineRun directly

' Provide payload JSON
TR --> Payload : supply payload
DirectExec --> Payload : supply payload
Payload --> PR : param: payload JSON

' User interactions
SRE --> CLI : run CAD workflows\n(e.g., CHGM)
Deploy --> EL : operate EventListener/Trigger
Deploy --> PR : manage PipelineRun
Dev --> TmplUtil : run updates
TmplUtil --> Templates : update manifests

' Notes for requirements
note right of CLI
- Provides cadctl entrypoint
- Performs CHGM workflow
- Detects anomalies and sends communications
- Executes mitigation/disposition actions
end note

note right of Tekton
Supports both execution paths:\n1) Webhook: EventListener -> Trigger -> PipelineRun\n2) Skip-webhook: direct PipelineRun creation
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Build: Go 1.17 builder\nImage: UBI minimal\nLabels: vendor, name, description, displayName,\nversion, build-date, VCS ref, Dockerfile path
end note

@enduml